Problem:
Let \( x_{1}, x_{2}, x_{3}, x_{4} \) be positive real numbers such that \( x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3} + x_{4} = \pi \). Find the minimum value of the expression

\[
\begin{array}{l}
\left(2 \sin^{2} x_{1} + \frac{1}{\sin^{2} x_{1}}\right) \cdot \left(2 \sin^{2} x_{2} + \frac{1}{\sin^{2} x_{2}}\right) \cdot \left(2 \sin^{2} x_{3} + \frac{1}{\sin^{2} x_{3}}\right) \cdot \left(2 \sin^{2} x_{4} + \frac{1}{\sin^{2} x_{4}}\right)
\end{array}
\]
